# Kernel tests compare the frozen corpus as raw UTF-8 bytes: corpus files must stay LF.
tools/UniversalSqueakerKernelTests/fixtures/corpus/*.txt text eol=lf

# Determinism, not style (same ruling as the carrier repo's .gitattributes). stage-package.ps1 copies
# LICENSE / About.xml / LoadFolders.xml byte-for-byte out of the working tree into the package, and
# release.yml prints the asset's SHA-256 into the public release body - the digest is only meaningful
# if every checkout of the same commit yields the same bytes. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows
# default, and what a windows-latest runner uses) a fresh clone turns LICENSE into 16127 bytes where
# the repository's own checkout has 15780 - 347 lines, 347 stray CRs. That is not cosmetic here:
# verify-local's licence gate compares US's LICENSE byte-for-byte against the carrier checkout, which
# pins LF, so a CRLF working tree fails the gate on the runner while passing locally. (Measured in a
# clean worktree simulation 2026-09-07; the local working tree had drifted LF by luck.)
#
# Index content is already LF, so this changes no stored file; it stops checkout from rewriting them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A gitignored DLL never enters a checkout, so these lines guard against a future asset being added by
# accident and silently re-encoded: byte-exact is the requirement for anything that ships inside a mod.
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.ogg binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.zip binary
*.nupkg binary

# Replays and fixtures compare as raw bytes; a converted line ending is a content change there.
fixtures/** text eol=lf
